<title>JAPAN: Gloomy earnings depress Yaohan Japan's shares.</title>
<headline>Gloomy earnings depress Yaohan Japan's shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gloomy earnings prospects depressed Yaohan Japan Corp's shares in Friday's morning session, brokers said, forcing the share price to a record low.</p>
<p>At the midday close, the shares were down 40 yen at 560 yen, the second sharpest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Earlier this week, the supermarket operator revised its parent current profit forecast for the year to March 31, 1997 to 2.68 billion yen from a previous forecast of 4.32 billion yen.</p>
